WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:49.960 --> 00:01:54.430
<b>Cape Promise</b>

3
00:02:06.860 --> 00:02:08.320
It's a...

4
00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:11.870
Flower?

5
00:02:13.280 --> 00:02:14.370
No it's...

6
00:02:14.440 --> 00:02:15.280
...a person...

7
00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:16.570
Are ya sure?

8
00:02:16.570 --> 00:02:19.470
That old man just
killed a Great King Squid

9
00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:20.120
with one shot!

10
00:02:20.120 --> 00:02:21.870
The question is, why...?

11
00:02:21.870 --> 00:02:23.800
Was he trying to save us?

12
00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:24.960
Or is he just fishing?

13
00:02:52.240 --> 00:02:54.700
You gonna say anything?

14
00:02:57.660 --> 00:03:00.200
Hey, you wanna fight,
we'll fight!

15
00:03:00.200 --> 00:03:01.910
We got cannons back
here, you bastard!

16
00:03:13.010 --> 00:03:15.880
You try it, and someone's
going to die.

17
00:03:19.540 --> 00:03:21.910
Yeah...? And who's that?

18
00:03:22.040 --> 00:03:23.080
Me, of course.

19
00:03:23.150 --> 00:03:24.650
'Scuse me?!

20
00:03:24.700 --> 00:03:25.230
You...!

21
00:03:25.230 --> 00:03:26.570
Ease up there, bud.

22
00:03:26.570 --> 00:03:28.610
The old bastard's mocking us!

23
00:03:29.770 --> 00:03:31.770
There's a couple things
we need to know...

24
00:03:31.770 --> 00:03:34.650
Where are we? And who are you?

25
00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:45.660
You've got some nerve stranger...

26
00:03:46.330 --> 00:03:47.180
It's only polite
to introduce yourself

27
00:03:47.250 --> 00:03:50.500
before asking a question
of someone you've just met.

28
00:03:50.500 --> 00:03:54.960
Uh. Heh. All right, fair enough.
I'll go first. My name...

29
00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:56.040
If you must know,

30
00:03:56.080 --> 00:03:57.680
my name is Crocus,

31
00:03:57.680 --> 00:04:00.890
and I'm the lighthouse
keeper of the Twin Capes...

32
00:04:00.890 --> 00:04:02.720
I'm 71-and-a-half years old...

33
00:04:02.780 --> 00:04:03.240
Gemini.

34
00:04:03.240 --> 00:04:04.410
I'll kill him! I swear it!

35
00:04:04.440 --> 00:04:05.390
Calm down.

36
00:04:05.390 --> 00:04:07.560
You'd like to know
where we are,

37
00:04:08.100 --> 00:04:10.210
but your rude behavior
leaves me disinclined

38
00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:12.140
to accommodate your curiosity,

39
00:04:12.140 --> 00:04:15.650
except that you are trespassing
on my private resort.

40
00:04:16.440 --> 00:04:18.580
Besides, I'd think
it's pretty obvious,

41
00:04:18.610 --> 00:04:20.820
seeing as how you were eaten.

42
00:04:21.140 --> 00:04:23.680
So you're saying that
we were swallowed by the whale,

43
00:04:23.840 --> 00:04:26.200
but since when does a whale's
stomach have clouds in it?

44
00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:27.440
Wait a minute!

45
00:04:27.480 --> 00:04:29.120
If we've been eaten,
what's gonna happen to us?!

46
00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:31.540
I don't wanna be digested!

47
00:04:39.510 --> 00:04:41.390
– Stop doing that!
– Stop doing that!

48
00:04:41.390 --> 00:04:42.180
What's wrong?

49
00:04:42.180 --> 00:04:44.100
Haven't you ever heard
of a "running gag"?

50
00:04:44.100 --> 00:04:44.970
That was a gag?!

51
00:04:44.970 --> 00:04:46.970
The exit is over there.

52
00:04:46.970 --> 00:04:48.480
– We can get out?!
– We can get out?!

53
00:04:49.280 --> 00:04:52.310
Okay, even if
I believed a whale's belly

54
00:04:52.380 --> 00:04:53.310
could have an exit door,

55
00:04:53.310 --> 00:04:55.190
nothing's there but sky!

56
00:04:55.190 --> 00:04:57.710
Something's not right here...

57
00:04:58.480 --> 00:04:59.980
Wait... Look at the sky...

58
00:05:00.180 --> 00:05:02.880
Those seagulls...
Nothing's moving.

59
00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:03.880
They're painted on!

60
00:05:04.080 --> 00:05:06.450
It's a giant mural inside
the whale's stomach!

61
00:05:06.450 --> 00:05:07.660
Huh?

62
00:05:07.660 --> 00:05:09.290
Call it a doctor's playful mind.

63
00:05:09.290 --> 00:05:11.670
You're not making any sense,
you crazy old fool!

64
00:05:11.670 --> 00:05:13.380
Easy. Don't let him get to you.

65
00:05:13.380 --> 00:05:14.460
Yeah, just shut up...

66
00:05:14.460 --> 00:05:15.740
Nami...

67
00:05:15.780 --> 00:05:17.000
If that is an exit,
then we need to get to it...

68
00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:18.420
Agreed.

69
00:05:23.050 --> 00:05:24.510
Aw, great! What now?!

70
00:05:25.890 --> 00:05:27.220
It's begun.

71
00:05:28.350 --> 00:05:29.230
Look!

72
00:05:30.020 --> 00:05:31.350
That's no island!

73
00:05:31.350 --> 00:05:33.650
It's some kind of ship!
It's made of iron!

74
00:05:33.650 --> 00:05:35.180
Yeah, of course!

75
00:05:35.220 --> 00:05:37.150
'Cause we're floating
on a sea of gastric acid!

76
00:05:37.150 --> 00:05:39.380
That means a wooden ship
wouldn't fare well

77
00:05:39.420 --> 00:05:40.820
if it stayed here too long.

78
00:05:40.820 --> 00:05:43.030
Hey! What's with
this freaky whale?!

79
00:05:43.030 --> 00:05:45.030
Answer me old man!

80
00:05:45.700 --> 00:05:47.200
He's very angry.

81
00:05:48.700 --> 00:05:50.980
These aftershocks
are a result of him

82
00:05:51.020 --> 00:05:53.170
hitting his head
against the Red Line.

83
00:06:02.590 --> 00:06:03.510
What?!

84
00:06:03.510 --> 00:06:04.750
That explains it...

85
00:06:04.980 --> 00:06:07.510
Why he had such deep
scars on his forehead.

86
00:06:07.510 --> 00:06:09.640
Not to mention all
the strange howling...

87
00:06:09.640 --> 00:06:11.230
Why's he do it?

88
00:06:12.100 --> 00:06:13.690
It's because he's suffering!

89
00:06:20.740 --> 00:06:21.950
It's all starting to make sense!

90
00:06:21.980 --> 00:06:24.110
So, what's the geezer up to?

91
00:06:24.110 --> 00:06:25.030
More than likely he's trying

92
00:06:25.030 --> 00:06:28.080
to kill the whale
from the inside...

93
00:06:28.080 --> 00:06:28.910
It's time.

94
00:06:28.910 --> 00:06:31.160
What a despicable
way to kill something.

95
00:06:31.280 --> 00:06:33.080
Okay, we've solved
the mystery of the whale.

96
00:06:33.080 --> 00:06:34.250
Now how about we find a way out

97
00:06:34.250 --> 00:06:35.370
of its belly before
it digests us.

98
00:06:36.540 --> 00:06:38.320
We have no right
to judge the old man,

99
00:06:38.320 --> 00:06:40.080
nor do we need
to save the whale.

100
00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:41.790
What we need to
do is focus on how

101
00:06:41.850 --> 00:06:44.220
to get the hell out of here...

102
00:06:57.060 --> 00:06:58.050
We're never gonna get anywhere

103
00:06:58.080 --> 00:07:00.520
if the waves keep
surging like this!

104
00:07:00.520 --> 00:07:02.650
How can we escape
if we can't even move?!

105
00:07:02.650 --> 00:07:04.950
Our only choice is
to paddle! Take the oars!

106
00:07:04.950 --> 00:07:06.580
Whatever it takes!

107
00:07:06.610 --> 00:07:07.910
We have to find
Luffy right away!

108
00:07:07.910 --> 00:07:09.280
I know he's outside!

109
00:07:09.280 --> 00:07:11.240
I caught a glimpse of him
flying out of the whale's mouth!

110
00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:16.000
That old guy just jumped in!

111
00:07:16.000 --> 00:07:16.790
Huh?

112
00:07:17.290 --> 00:07:18.710
Is he insane?

113
00:07:18.710 --> 00:07:19.790
The acid will eat him alive.

114
00:07:27.460 --> 00:07:31.730
Aaaah!

115
00:07:32.560 --> 00:07:36.190
So dizzy! I'm gonna hurl.

116
00:07:44.190 --> 00:07:45.440
Hey, that's weird...

117
00:07:45.440 --> 00:07:48.240
The whale's got
a river inside it, too?

118
00:07:58.300 --> 00:07:59.870
Things are looking up, my dear!

119
00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:02.100
We've been successful so far.

120
00:08:02.100 --> 00:08:04.110
Listen carefully,
Miss Wednesday...

121
00:08:02.210 --> 00:08:04.630
<b>Miss Wednesday
Mysterious Woman</b>

122
00:08:04.300 --> 00:08:06.840
Behind these doors
lie the beast's stomach,

123
00:08:06.910 --> 00:08:09.510
and that troublesome
geezer as well.

124
00:08:09.510 --> 00:08:12.140
He must be eliminated
before he can interfere again.

125
00:08:12.180 --> 00:08:15.020
<b>Mr. 9
Mysterious Man</b>

126
00:08:12.760 --> 00:08:15.020
Remember... it's all
for the whale.

127
00:08:15.390 --> 00:08:17.020
Indeed, Mr. 9...

128
00:08:17.020 --> 00:08:18.870
This whale's
a precious creature,

129
00:08:18.910 --> 00:08:21.480
and one that holds the sweet
promise of life for our town.

130
00:08:24.230 --> 00:08:26.320
Guys! Crocus just resurfaced!

131
00:08:26.320 --> 00:08:27.320
Look, forget about the old guy!

132
00:08:27.320 --> 00:08:30.820
Our focus should be on finding
a way to open these doors.

133
00:08:31.280 --> 00:08:33.830
All right...

134
00:08:33.830 --> 00:08:36.330
Here's the plan baby.
"Three... Two... One..."

135
00:08:36.330 --> 00:08:37.460
Then we kick through the doors.

136
00:08:37.460 --> 00:08:39.290
Roger that, Mr. 9.

137
00:08:39.290 --> 00:08:40.420
I'm ready any time.

138
00:08:44.100 --> 00:08:45.830
What is that voice, Mr. 9?

139
00:08:45.900 --> 00:08:47.830
I don't know, Miss Wednesday.

140
00:08:47.900 --> 00:08:50.960
I can't stop!

141
00:08:58.310 --> 00:08:59.440
They're back...

142
00:09:01.980 --> 00:09:06.940
Not good! We're
gonna fall into gastric acid!

143
00:09:08.340 --> 00:09:09.000
Luffy?

144
00:09:09.060 --> 00:09:11.170
Zoro! Is everyone okay?

145
00:09:12.670 --> 00:09:16.200
So, um... I could use a hand!

146
00:09:19.670 --> 00:09:20.940
Looks like Luffy's not alone...

147
00:09:21.170 --> 00:09:23.170
Who do you suppose the
two weirdoes are with him?

148
00:09:23.170 --> 00:09:25.340
Where'd that old geezer
disappear to?!

149
00:09:25.570 --> 00:09:27.800
Forget him...
We need to save Luffy!

150
00:09:43.100 --> 00:09:44.910
You've got to stop it, Laboon.

151
00:09:45.000 --> 00:09:47.900
You can't afford to beat
yourself up any more...

152
00:09:47.900 --> 00:09:50.240
There's only a tiny
amount of sedative left.

153
00:09:50.240 --> 00:09:54.010
And until I can make some
more you'll have to make nice.

154
00:09:55.950 --> 00:09:57.140
I've told you before...

155
00:09:57.170 --> 00:09:59.540
that wall divides
the world's oceans.

156
00:09:59.540 --> 00:10:02.170
It doesn't matter how
many times you hit it...

157
00:10:02.170 --> 00:10:03.070
It won't break.

158
00:10:03.110 --> 00:10:04.540
Not even for someone
as mighty as you.

159
00:10:09.460 --> 00:10:10.840
I don't claim to speak whale,

160
00:10:10.840 --> 00:10:12.590
but it seems to
have calmed down a bit.

161
00:10:12.590 --> 00:10:14.470
Seems that way.

162
00:10:17.010 --> 00:10:19.110
Now, we saved your lives
for the time being,

163
00:10:19.140 --> 00:10:20.560
but you'd better talk
and make it quick!

164
00:10:21.390 --> 00:10:24.350
Mr. 9, these
heathens are pirates!

165
00:10:24.350 --> 00:10:26.520
Yes, that's painfully
obvious, Miss Wednesday.

166
00:10:27.230 --> 00:10:29.240
But, if we speak to their
humanity and compassion,

167
00:10:29.310 --> 00:10:32.030
they should understand our
plight... Maybe.

168
00:10:32.030 --> 00:10:34.490
You parasites are still here?!

169
00:10:35.200 --> 00:10:37.410
I grow weary of this,
and for the last time!

170
00:10:37.990 --> 00:10:39.940
As long as I draw breath,

171
00:10:40.030 --> 00:10:42.580
you will not lay a single,
harmful finger on Laboon!

172
00:10:45.170 --> 00:10:46.380
He's back again.

173
00:10:46.800 --> 00:10:47.940
Who's the old guy?

174
00:10:50.300 --> 00:10:52.630
You can't bully us into
abandoning our mission.

175
00:10:52.920 --> 00:10:54.270
We were sent
here to hunt this whale,

176
00:10:54.300 --> 00:10:55.630
and that's exactly
what we're going to do!

177
00:10:55.630 --> 00:10:58.510
And this time,
we won't let you interfere!

178
00:10:58.510 --> 00:11:01.560
We're about to give
this whale a new blowhole!

179
00:11:01.900 --> 00:11:02.970
Fire, baby!

180
00:11:03.010 --> 00:11:04.370
Roger!

181
00:11:15.490 --> 00:11:17.660
He jumped straight
into the line of fire!

182
00:11:17.660 --> 00:11:20.160
Did he just... Was he
protecting the whale?!

183
00:11:23.580 --> 00:11:25.120
Go ahead... Waste your time!

184
00:11:27.920 --> 00:11:29.720
But, make no mistake...

185
00:11:29.760 --> 00:11:31.940
That hulking beast will
provide food for our town!

186
00:11:37.720 --> 00:11:39.060
What's going on?

187
00:11:46.390 --> 00:11:47.900
Um... What was that for?

188
00:11:54.070 --> 00:11:55.420
I thank you for saving my life,

189
00:11:55.460 --> 00:11:56.520
though I must ask...

190
00:11:56.630 --> 00:11:57.820
Why did you do it?

191
00:11:57.820 --> 00:11:59.410
I wasn't trying to save you...

192
00:11:59.410 --> 00:12:01.700
There was just something
about those two I didn't like.

193
00:12:02.090 --> 00:12:03.120
Oh...

194
00:12:03.120 --> 00:12:04.920
Okay, I think it's
time we got some answers.

195
00:12:05.520 --> 00:12:06.760
Who are these guys?

196
00:12:06.920 --> 00:12:09.020
And how did you
end up inside this whale?

197
00:12:09.020 --> 00:12:11.120
These two are
thugs from a nearby town,

198
00:12:11.160 --> 00:12:12.220
looking for whale meat...

199
00:12:12.620 --> 00:12:14.990
If they caught him, Laboon
could feed the townspeople

200
00:12:15.020 --> 00:12:17.420
for at least 2 or 3 years, easy.

201
00:12:17.420 --> 00:12:18.620
All they're concerned with

202
00:12:18.620 --> 00:12:21.290
is filling their
fat, greedy bellies!

203
00:12:21.420 --> 00:12:22.050
Laboon?

204
00:12:22.050 --> 00:12:24.140
That's the whale's name.

205
00:12:24.140 --> 00:12:26.820
He's a unique and
magnificent creature...

206
00:12:26.820 --> 00:12:29.480
An island whale one of the
largest species in the world

207
00:12:29.480 --> 00:12:32.230
that can only be found
in the West Blue...

208
00:12:32.230 --> 00:12:35.360
I won't allow them to
slaughter him for food.

209
00:12:35.720 --> 00:12:37.020
It's a shame that
he's stuck here

210
00:12:37.060 --> 00:12:39.190
so far away from his domain...

211
00:12:39.320 --> 00:12:41.560
You see, there's a reason
he keeps hitting himself

212
00:12:41.560 --> 00:12:44.330
on the Red Line and
howling at Reverse Mountain.

213
00:12:44.330 --> 00:12:45.080
There is?

214
00:12:45.080 --> 00:12:46.290
Yes... To put it one way...

215
00:12:46.660 --> 00:12:52.210
Inside Laboon's body
beats the heart of a human...

216
00:12:52.630 --> 00:12:55.120
He has most impatiently awaited

217
00:12:55.160 --> 00:12:57.630
and is eternally devoted to
a certain band of pirates...

218
00:13:01.300 --> 00:13:03.510
Going on 50 long years now.

219
00:13:03.970 --> 00:13:06.520
Listen closely,

220
00:13:06.590 --> 00:13:08.480
and I will reveal to you
Laboon's tragic story.

221
00:13:21.990 --> 00:13:24.490
One fine sunny day,

222
00:13:24.520 --> 00:13:26.660
while I was fulfilling my duties
as the lighthouse keeper,

223
00:13:26.660 --> 00:13:31.040
some good-natured pirates
came down Reverse Mountain.

224
00:13:33.710 --> 00:13:35.690
They were followed by a
baby whale, spry and chipper,

225
00:13:35.690 --> 00:13:40.920
whom I would soon come to know
as the one and only, Laboon.

226
00:13:41.760 --> 00:13:45.970
He is an Island Whale,
one of the largest in the world.

227
00:13:45.970 --> 00:13:47.640
They are a rare species
found only in the West Blue.

228
00:13:48.640 --> 00:13:51.020
Laboon had developed
a bond with the pirates,

229
00:13:51.060 --> 00:13:52.640
traveling with them
for much of their journey.

230
00:13:52.640 --> 00:13:55.220
But knowing the dangers
of the Grand Line,

231
00:13:55.260 --> 00:13:59.360
the pirates chose to leave
Laboon behind in the West Blue.

232
00:13:59.360 --> 00:14:01.780
But the stubborn little
whale followed them anyway.

233
00:14:02.780 --> 00:14:05.990
As a general rule, Island
Whales are social animals,

234
00:14:06.020 --> 00:14:07.830
and travel together
in family groups.

235
00:14:08.370 --> 00:14:10.920
I suspect that Laboon
had somehow come to feel

236
00:14:10.960 --> 00:14:13.290
that those pirates
were his family.

237
00:14:13.290 --> 00:14:16.960
The wear and tear on the
pirates' ship was quite severe,

238
00:14:16.960 --> 00:14:18.630
so they stayed here
for several months.

239
00:14:18.630 --> 00:14:21.120
In that time, I, too, was able

240
00:14:21.160 --> 00:14:22.380
to forge a close
relationship with them.

241
00:14:24.010 --> 00:14:26.970
Thus, when the day of their
departure finally arrived.

242
00:14:27.600 --> 00:14:29.600
I have a favor to ask
of you, my dear friend.

243
00:14:29.600 --> 00:14:32.230
Could you look after
Laboon for a few years?

244
00:14:32.770 --> 00:14:34.560
When my men and I have completed

245
00:14:34.590 --> 00:14:36.310
our voyage around the world,
we'll be back.

246
00:14:37.440 --> 00:14:40.110
Listen to me, Laboon...

247
00:14:40.110 --> 00:14:43.700
We're taking our ship to
the end of the Grand Line.

248
00:14:43.700 --> 00:14:46.120
Until we return, I need you
to wait for us here with Crocus.

249
00:14:46.450 --> 00:14:48.370
You can't come with us...

250
00:14:48.370 --> 00:14:50.700
It's too dangerous, even
for a mighty whale like you.

251
00:14:51.330 --> 00:14:54.160
Don't worry three years
will pass by like a flash.

252
00:14:54.160 --> 00:14:55.420
And don't forget...

253
00:14:55.920 --> 00:14:58.670
No matter the distance,
our friendship lasts forever.

254
00:15:03.130 --> 00:15:04.630
Well, I guess it's time!

255
00:15:08.390 --> 00:15:10.470
All right, men!

256
00:15:10.470 --> 00:15:12.020
We're setting sail!
Hoist the anchor!

257
00:15:17.690 --> 00:15:18.940
Laboon!

258
00:15:20.150 --> 00:15:22.230
You have to wait for us here
and mind Crocus, Laboon.

259
00:15:22.230 --> 00:15:24.700
Don't worry we'll be back...

260
00:15:24.700 --> 00:15:26.320
I promise.

261
00:15:38.880 --> 00:15:41.800
That was fifty long years ago.

262
00:15:41.800 --> 00:15:43.050
Fifty years?!

263
00:15:43.050 --> 00:15:45.200
So, Laboon has been
waiting all this time

264
00:15:45.260 --> 00:15:46.430
for his friends to return...

265
00:15:46.430 --> 00:15:48.230
No wonder he's upset...

266
00:15:48.230 --> 00:15:50.470
That kind of wait
would drive anyone crazy!

267
00:16:00.690 --> 00:16:02.440
This is some canal...

268
00:16:02.440 --> 00:16:03.760
Amazing this
whale's still alive,

269
00:16:03.800 --> 00:16:05.490
with a hole like
this in his body.

270
00:16:05.490 --> 00:16:07.110
I suppose you're
responsible for this?

271
00:16:07.110 --> 00:16:08.950
Just a doctor's playful mind...

272
00:16:08.950 --> 00:16:09.820
Doctor?!

273
00:16:09.820 --> 00:16:11.030
That's right.

274
00:16:11.060 --> 00:16:12.080
Legally certified...

275
00:16:12.080 --> 00:16:15.330
I also ran a clinic on
the cape once upon a time.

276
00:16:15.330 --> 00:16:17.960
Before that, I served
as a ship's doctor.

277
00:16:17.960 --> 00:16:19.170
Really?

278
00:16:19.670 --> 00:16:20.230
That's great...

279
00:16:20.230 --> 00:16:21.750
Then join us,
we need a doctor.

280
00:16:21.750 --> 00:16:23.550
Don't be ridiculous.

281
00:16:23.550 --> 00:16:26.130
I no longer have
that kind of energy.

282
00:16:26.130 --> 00:16:27.720
Exploring the seas is
a young man's burden.

283
00:16:27.720 --> 00:16:30.100
What kind of a doctor
hollows out

284
00:16:30.130 --> 00:16:31.010
the inside of a whale...

285
00:16:31.010 --> 00:16:32.720
Maybe it's part of
the treatment.

286
00:16:33.180 --> 00:16:34.720
The girl is right...

287
00:16:34.720 --> 00:16:35.800
With a creature of this size,

288
00:16:35.800 --> 00:16:38.630
it's virtually impossible to
treat it from the outside.

289
00:16:38.630 --> 00:16:41.400
Therefore, I devised a more
drastic solution.

290
00:16:41.530 --> 00:16:43.100
Here's the exit...

291
00:16:53.450 --> 00:16:57.620
The sky.

292
00:17:06.420 --> 00:17:08.300
What is it?

293
00:17:10.550 --> 00:17:12.720
Don't you think
fifty years is a bit extreme?

294
00:17:12.720 --> 00:17:15.180
Those pirates sure know how
to test someone's patience!

295
00:17:15.180 --> 00:17:16.430
Idiot! Don't ya get it?

296
00:17:16.430 --> 00:17:18.520
This is the Grand Line.

297
00:17:18.850 --> 00:17:20.270
His friends are dead.

298
00:17:23.240 --> 00:17:25.310
Ugh! Why are you all
being so pessimistic?

299
00:17:25.340 --> 00:17:26.540
You don't know
that they're dead!

300
00:17:26.740 --> 00:17:28.540
They could still
come back for him!

301
00:17:28.540 --> 00:17:30.640
Come on. Have some
sympathy, will ya?!

302
00:17:30.640 --> 00:17:32.360
I thought it was very touching!

303
00:17:32.360 --> 00:17:33.670
I mean a whale still
believing a promise

304
00:17:33.710 --> 00:17:35.580
his friends made
despite all these years?!

305
00:17:35.580 --> 00:17:37.700
That's a true bond!
Right, pops?!

306
00:17:37.700 --> 00:17:39.040
Indeed...

307
00:17:39.040 --> 00:17:42.290
But the lesson here
is that reality is cruel.

308
00:17:42.290 --> 00:17:44.410
Laboon's cohorts aren't dead.

309
00:17:44.440 --> 00:17:46.920
The truth is, they
abandoned their quest.

310
00:17:46.920 --> 00:17:50.010
I learned that they turned tail
and left the Grand Line.

311
00:17:50.010 --> 00:17:51.550
I don't believe it.

312
00:17:51.550 --> 00:17:54.470
I mean, why abandon
him like that?

313
00:17:55.720 --> 00:17:57.810
You say they ran
away from the Grand Line.

314
00:17:57.810 --> 00:18:00.180
Do you know if they made it
through the Calm Belt alive?

315
00:18:00.180 --> 00:18:02.640
I can't claim to know
exactly what became of them,

316
00:18:02.640 --> 00:18:05.110
but I doubt they'll ever
come back here again.

317
00:18:06.240 --> 00:18:10.210
Seasons, weather, currents, wind
direction... on the Grand Line,

318
00:18:10.240 --> 00:18:13.740
these elements seem to
defy the very laws of nature.

319
00:18:13.740 --> 00:18:15.580
Common sense is useless,

320
00:18:15.610 --> 00:18:19.010
and the terror of that fact
can be quite overwhelming.

321
00:18:19.140 --> 00:18:21.010
So, if I've got this straight,
what you're saying is,

322
00:18:21.040 --> 00:18:22.410
these pirates were
a bunch of cowards,

323
00:18:22.410 --> 00:18:24.670
who cared more about
saving their own asses,

324
00:18:24.670 --> 00:18:26.290
than keeping a
promise to a friend?

325
00:18:28.090 --> 00:18:30.840
Why would anyone abandon
such a loyal creature?!

326
00:18:30.840 --> 00:18:33.470
Just look at him!

327
00:18:33.470 --> 00:18:34.680
It's cruelty on a grand scale!

328
00:18:35.220 --> 00:18:38.470
But if you've known all this,
why haven't you told him?

329
00:18:38.810 --> 00:18:41.600
Laboon can obviously
communicate with you.

330
00:18:41.930 --> 00:18:43.270
He seems to understand
humans quite well for a whale.

331
00:18:43.270 --> 00:18:43.870
I did tell him...

332
00:18:43.910 --> 00:18:45.730
...down to the last,
miserable detail.

333
00:18:46.310 --> 00:18:48.520
I know this isn't what you want
to hear, but it's the truth.

334
00:18:48.520 --> 00:18:51.570
Your friends left
the Grand Line.

335
00:18:52.110 --> 00:18:54.450
The bond you shared
with each other was real.

336
00:18:54.780 --> 00:18:58.450
Just as real as the promise they
made to return for you one day.

337
00:19:04.540 --> 00:19:06.330
But, still... face the facts...

338
00:19:06.920 --> 00:19:08.840
Those men are
never coming back.

339
00:19:29.110 --> 00:19:31.780
Laboon! Please!

340
00:19:31.780 --> 00:19:33.490
I say this for your own good!
They're not coming back!

341
00:19:42.580 --> 00:19:45.250
I understand that
you don't wanna accept it!

342
00:19:46.000 --> 00:19:49.380
But you need to realize
that this is how things are!

343
00:19:50.360 --> 00:19:51.660
Listen...

344
00:19:55.300 --> 00:19:56.840
Laboon!

345
00:20:07.100 --> 00:20:09.310
That was the day
that Laboon began

346
00:20:09.490 --> 00:20:12.940
to howl at Reverse Mountain...

347
00:20:12.940 --> 00:20:16.570
Soon after, he started slamming
his body against the Red Line.

348
00:20:16.570 --> 00:20:18.490
It's as if he believes that wall
is what keeps his friends away,

349
00:20:18.490 --> 00:20:23.240
and by breaking it, he can
clear the path for their return.

350
00:20:23.830 --> 00:20:25.120
I admire his dedication...

351
00:20:25.120 --> 00:20:27.290
Never gave up on 'em.

352
00:20:27.290 --> 00:20:28.760
He refuses to believe me,

353
00:20:28.790 --> 00:20:31.760
because then he'd have
to admit that it's over.

354
00:20:31.860 --> 00:20:34.560
And that terrifies him
more than anything.

355
00:20:34.560 --> 00:20:36.960
There's no way for him to
go back to the West Blue...

356
00:20:37.260 --> 00:20:41.030
So, what we have is a
paradox of tragic proportions.

357
00:20:41.090 --> 00:20:44.820
Laboon is a lost soul dying
to live with his friends,

358
00:20:44.820 --> 00:20:46.730
but won't stop killing
himself to reach them...

359
00:20:46.730 --> 00:20:50.730
Tragedy. Still for all the grief
those pirates put him through

360
00:20:50.730 --> 00:20:53.520
they did the same to you by
saddling you with their burden.

361
00:20:55.860 --> 00:20:58.080
I mean you've done
enough for Laboon.

362
00:20:58.110 --> 00:20:58.910
What about you...?

363
00:20:58.910 --> 00:21:00.940
The scars on his hide are deep.

364
00:21:01.110 --> 00:21:03.280
Those in his heart
are even deeper...

365
00:21:03.310 --> 00:21:05.180
He needs someone
to tend his wounds,

366
00:21:05.240 --> 00:21:06.540
and I'm all he's got...

367
00:21:06.540 --> 00:21:10.110
For years, he's battered himself
while I've patched him up...

368
00:21:10.110 --> 00:21:12.640
A strange friendship,
but it works.

369
00:21:14.750 --> 00:21:16.380
What the hell
is that idiot up to?

370
00:21:16.380 --> 00:21:18.130
Ya gotta watch
him every second...

371
00:21:18.130 --> 00:21:20.090
We've been watching him,
look what happens...

372
00:21:21.890 --> 00:21:24.510
Gum-Gum...

373
00:21:24.510 --> 00:21:26.600
...Flower Arrangement!

374
00:21:26.930 --> 00:21:28.730
Think he's aware
that's our mast...?

375
00:21:28.730 --> 00:21:30.730
And now it's on top of a whale.

376
00:21:30.730 --> 00:21:32.020
Why'd he do that?

377
00:21:32.350 --> 00:21:34.650
Hey Luffy, stop
tearing up the ship.

378
00:21:41.900 --> 00:21:44.810
You... ass...! Luffy... stop...!

379
00:21:54.710 --> 00:21:55.790
The boy...! He's dead!

380
00:21:56.170 --> 00:21:57.100
Oh don't worry...!

381
00:21:57.300 --> 00:21:59.210
It'll take way more
than that to kill Luffy!

382
00:22:04.010 --> 00:22:04.850
Ha...! Gotcha!

383
00:22:11.600 --> 00:22:13.020
What does he
think he's doing?!

384
00:22:17.070 --> 00:22:19.060
You wanna let us in on your plan

385
00:22:19.060 --> 00:22:20.240
before ya kill yourself?!

386
00:22:25.070 --> 00:22:26.200
It's a draw!

387
00:22:31.000 --> 00:22:32.290
I'm stronger than I look!

388
00:22:34.370 --> 00:22:36.790
I can always tell when
someone's itching to fight...

389
00:22:36.790 --> 00:22:38.800
Well, if you want a battle,
I'll gladly give you one...

390
00:22:38.800 --> 00:22:42.380
Your shipmates used to
spar with you, didn't they?

391
00:22:42.380 --> 00:22:43.460
You miss it.

392
00:22:43.460 --> 00:22:46.600
Well, I can rival
anything they threw at ya!

393
00:22:46.960 --> 00:22:47.930
Tell ya what...

394
00:22:47.960 --> 00:22:49.830
after me and my friends
travel the Grand Line,

395
00:22:49.900 --> 00:22:51.660
we'll come back
here and find you.

396
00:22:51.730 --> 00:22:58.440
And then you better be
ready for a rematch!

397
00:23:09.280 --> 00:23:10.450
Hey, not bad!

398
00:23:10.450 --> 00:23:12.480
Consider this a
symbol of my promise

399
00:23:12.510 --> 00:23:14.330
to come do battle with you...

400
00:23:14.330 --> 00:23:15.680
Of course, it's a
rush paint job,

401
00:23:15.680 --> 00:23:18.350
so you'll have to be careful
and avoid hitting your head

402
00:23:18.350 --> 00:23:19.350
or you'll rub it right off.

403
00:23:19.370 --> 00:23:20.340
Understand?

404
00:23:23.760 --> 00:23:25.510
Good whale!

405
00:23:27.390 --> 00:23:28.510
Where are they?

406
00:23:28.510 --> 00:23:31.850
Where are who...?
Oh, you mean those two weirdoes?

407
00:23:31.850 --> 00:23:33.350
I guess they escaped.

408
00:23:33.350 --> 00:23:35.710
Must have happened when
we were distracted by Laboon.

409
00:23:35.710 --> 00:23:36.650
I wonder who they were...

410
00:23:39.560 --> 00:23:41.130
Miss Wednesday...

411
00:23:41.130 --> 00:23:42.860
What are we going to do now?

412
00:23:45.150 --> 00:23:47.000
First, put some
distance between us

413
00:23:47.030 --> 00:23:47.670
and these morons.

414
00:23:47.760 --> 00:23:49.000
Then we report to the Boss.

415
00:23:49.030 --> 00:23:52.030
Our time for completing this
mission has long since run out.

416
00:23:52.030 --> 00:23:53.370
I can hear the others now.

417
00:23:53.430 --> 00:23:55.620
They're probably
already calling us traitors.

418
00:23:56.000 --> 00:23:56.750
I know...

419
00:23:56.750 --> 00:23:57.800
But without our weapons,

420
00:23:58.030 --> 00:24:00.090
we've no choice but to go back
to the office and start over.

421
00:24:00.090 --> 00:24:04.210
And this time no
one will stop us...

422
00:24:04.210 --> 00:24:05.760
Aaaah!

423
00:24:05.760 --> 00:24:06.550
No, no! I couldn't have!

424
00:24:06.880 --> 00:24:07.880
What is it?

425
00:24:09.430 --> 00:24:10.140
It's... gone.

426
00:24:10.140 --> 00:24:10.760
What?!

427
00:24:11.580 --> 00:24:12.880
Huh?

428
00:24:13.520 --> 00:24:14.430
Hmm... What's this thing?

429
00:24:15.180 --> 00:24:17.230
How could you have
lost the Log Pose?!

430
00:24:17.230 --> 00:24:18.470
I don't know!

431
00:24:18.730 --> 00:24:20.730
I must've dropped it somewhere!

432
00:24:20.730 --> 00:24:23.500
But we're not going
anywhere without it...

433
00:24:23.630 --> 00:24:25.500
- How awful!

434
00:24:25.860 --> 00:24:28.240
Ah! No! This can't
be happening...

435
00:24:28.240 --> 00:24:28.950
Wha...?!

436
00:24:30.530 --> 00:24:31.780
It's...! Ahhhh...

437
00:24:32.740 --> 00:24:34.700
Oh no!

438
00:24:35.620 --> 00:24:36.910
The Unluckies!

439
00:24:36.910 --> 00:24:38.210
We're out of time!

440
00:24:37.330 --> 00:24:41.130
<b>Miss Friday

Mysterious
Vulture Mr. 13

Mysterious
Sea Otter</b>

441
00:24:38.210 --> 00:24:39.290
Mr. 13!

442
00:24:39.290 --> 00:24:41.130
Miss Friday!

443
00:24:41.460 --> 00:24:42.430
Don't be hasty!

444
00:24:42.430 --> 00:24:43.800
Please, we can explain!

445
00:24:44.030 --> 00:24:46.070
We'll check in with
Boss immediately!

446
00:24:46.130 --> 00:24:47.340
Aaaah!

447
00:25:00.650 --> 00:25:02.230
Okay, then!

448
00:25:02.270 --> 00:25:03.370
I finally have some
peace and quiet

449
00:25:03.370 --> 00:25:04.980
so I can work on a plan
for the Grand Line journey.

450
00:25:09.780 --> 00:25:13.660
Ah... Don't think I forgot about
you, Elephant Blue Fin Tuna!

451
00:25:13.660 --> 00:25:15.160
Damn... That's my life...!

452
00:25:16.120 --> 00:25:20.120
Luffy breaks it then
I put it back together!

453
00:25:20.120 --> 00:25:21.420
Hey, get off your lazy butt
and give me a hand!

454
00:25:21.420 --> 00:25:24.210
This ship isn't gonna
fix itself you know!

455
00:25:30.130 --> 00:25:31.720
You mind? Keep it down.

456
00:25:31.720 --> 00:25:33.600
Is there some problem,
my dearest Nami?!

457
00:25:33.600 --> 00:25:35.760
If it's food you're worried
about, say no more!

458
00:25:35.760 --> 00:25:36.560
Someone say "food"?

459
00:25:36.890 --> 00:25:39.020
You idiots!
The compass is broken!

460
00:25:39.640 --> 00:25:41.230
The needle just spins!
It won't stop!

461
00:25:41.230 --> 00:25:42.900
Oh, yeah, you're right.

462
00:25:42.900 --> 00:25:45.020
I don't know about you,
but I'm getting dizzy!

463
00:25:45.020 --> 00:25:46.690
Whoa... This is cool!

464
00:25:47.570 --> 00:25:49.450
It is sadly apparent
that none of you

465
00:25:49.510 --> 00:25:51.490
possess the slightest knowledge
about how things work here...

466
00:25:51.490 --> 00:25:54.570
Did you all come here to die?

467
00:25:55.030 --> 00:25:56.370
Ah, great spread!

468
00:25:56.370 --> 00:25:58.200
It's for everyone!

469
00:25:58.200 --> 00:25:59.660
There is nothing
wrong with your compass.

470
00:25:59.660 --> 00:26:03.080
The Grand Line has little
regard for the rules of the sea.

471
00:26:03.080 --> 00:26:06.380
Common sense is
useless in this place.

472
00:26:07.170 --> 00:26:09.380
The needle... Why does it spin?

473
00:26:09.380 --> 00:26:10.470
Because we are surrounded

474
00:26:10.470 --> 00:26:12.650
by a powerful magnetic field.

475
00:26:13.040 --> 00:26:15.850
The islands here are riddled
with magnetic minerals,

476
00:26:15.850 --> 00:26:18.600
which cause all
sorts of abnormalities.

477
00:26:18.740 --> 00:26:21.450
Also, the winds and
currents lack constancy

478
00:26:21.510 --> 00:26:22.680
in their patterns.

479
00:26:22.740 --> 00:26:26.340
As a navigator, I'm sure you
can appreciate this dilemma.

480
00:26:26.340 --> 00:26:27.180
So then...

481
00:26:27.210 --> 00:26:28.780
If we don't have
a way to tell direction,

482
00:26:28.810 --> 00:26:30.070
this whole trip is hopeless...

483
00:26:30.070 --> 00:26:31.030
Yummy!

484
00:26:31.340 --> 00:26:32.510
I don't know what to say...

485
00:26:32.540 --> 00:26:33.340
We're screwed...

486
00:26:33.340 --> 00:26:35.880
Hey! You're the navigator,
so navigate us outta here!

487
00:26:35.880 --> 00:26:38.020
This is delicious!
You oughta try some!

488
00:26:38.240 --> 00:26:39.850
Would all of you just
shut up for five seconds

489
00:26:39.880 --> 00:26:41.200
so I can figure this out!

490
00:26:41.310 --> 00:26:44.180
This nose of the Elephant
Tuna is my favorite part!

491
00:26:44.180 --> 00:26:45.210
Tasty!

492
00:26:45.240 --> 00:26:47.350
If you have any hope of
navigating the Grand Line,

493
00:26:47.380 --> 00:26:49.840
you're going to need
a Log Pose to guide you.

494
00:26:49.840 --> 00:26:51.210
Log Pose?

495
00:26:51.240 --> 00:26:52.090
I've never heard of it.

496
00:26:52.090 --> 00:26:53.580
It's a specially
designed compass

497
00:26:53.610 --> 00:26:56.090
that can record levels
of magnetism.

498
00:26:56.090 --> 00:26:57.640
Is it strange looking?

499
00:26:57.640 --> 00:27:00.220
Why, yes, it does
have an odd shape.

500
00:27:00.220 --> 00:27:01.640
Something like this?

501
00:27:01.640 --> 00:27:02.770
Yes, exactly...

502
00:27:03.230 --> 00:27:05.850
Only a fool courting
disaster would attempt

503
00:27:05.880 --> 00:27:08.150
to travel the
Grand Line without one.

504
00:27:08.900 --> 00:27:10.400
Understood...

505
00:27:10.400 --> 00:27:12.150
Excuse me for one second.

506
00:27:12.650 --> 00:27:14.070
So...

507
00:27:14.450 --> 00:27:17.070
Why didn't you tell me you
had one of those Log things?!

508
00:27:18.780 --> 00:27:20.540
I found it on deck,
just laying there.

509
00:27:20.540 --> 00:27:22.870
Those two weirdoes must've
dropped it when they escaped.

510
00:27:22.870 --> 00:27:24.040
Did they?

511
00:27:24.040 --> 00:27:25.420
Why'd you hit me?

512
00:27:25.420 --> 00:27:26.370
Felt like it...

513
00:27:26.370 --> 00:27:27.330
Oh, okay.

514
00:27:28.590 --> 00:27:31.460
Huh, but there isn't a
dial face on this thing.

515
00:27:31.460 --> 00:27:34.280
You don't need one.
It's a special brand

516
00:27:34.310 --> 00:27:36.650
of magnetism that runs
through the Grand Line islands.

517
00:27:36.840 --> 00:27:39.050
Complete with its own set of
rules that makes it possible

518
00:27:39.510 --> 00:27:41.020
to get around.

519
00:27:41.040 --> 00:27:44.230
By recording the level of
magnetism between two islands,

520
00:27:44.230 --> 00:27:46.730
you can chart a route
from one island to the next.

521
00:27:47.440 --> 00:27:50.350
The log pose method
is really the only choice.

522
00:27:50.410 --> 00:27:52.780
Since the magnetism here
presents huge problems

523
00:27:52.980 --> 00:27:54.940
for conventional navigation...

524
00:27:54.940 --> 00:27:58.540
As it turns out Reverse Mountain
is a great starting point.

525
00:27:58.540 --> 00:28:01.370
It produces seven
levels of magnetism.

526
00:28:01.370 --> 00:28:04.290
But it doesn't matter which one
you choose to start with.

527
00:28:04.290 --> 00:28:06.650
Eventually all of them
will pull against each other

528
00:28:06.680 --> 00:28:08.170
and form one route.

529
00:28:08.170 --> 00:28:11.710
And the island at the
end of that route...

530
00:28:12.210 --> 00:28:13.550
...is Raftel.

531
00:28:13.550 --> 00:28:16.340
The last and most mysterious
in the Grand Line...

532
00:28:16.340 --> 00:28:17.240
Its very existence
was confirmed

533
00:28:17.300 --> 00:28:20.240
by the King of the Pirates,
the only known person

534
00:28:20.310 --> 00:28:22.680
to have traveled the
Grand Line in its entirety.

535
00:28:22.680 --> 00:28:24.060
Raftel...

536
00:28:24.440 --> 00:28:25.140
That's it!

537
00:28:25.140 --> 00:28:26.980
That must be where
the One Piece is hidden...

538
00:28:27.140 --> 00:28:28.810
That's the most
prominent theory,

539
00:28:29.940 --> 00:28:32.650
but no one's been able to
set foot on Raftel Island since.

540
00:28:32.650 --> 00:28:35.820
Don't worry.
We'll know soon enough!

541
00:28:38.700 --> 00:28:40.340
Well, I'm satisfied!

542
00:28:40.340 --> 00:28:41.410
You guys ready to go?

543
00:28:41.410 --> 00:28:43.240
I told you that
was for all of us!

544
00:28:43.240 --> 00:28:44.910
He... He even ate the bones!

545
00:28:44.910 --> 00:28:46.180
A Log Pose...

546
00:28:46.440 --> 00:28:48.210
We have to take
special care of this...

547
00:28:48.210 --> 00:28:50.420
It's the key to finding the
greatest treasure of all time!

548
00:28:50.420 --> 00:28:52.170
You greedy, bottomless pit!

549
00:28:52.170 --> 00:28:54.800
You ate the meal
I made for Nami!

550
00:28:55.590 --> 00:28:58.720
Well I hope you left room...
for your dessert!

551
00:29:13.610 --> 00:29:14.570
Ow! Why's everyone hitting me?!

552
00:29:14.710 --> 00:29:16.410
You never think of
anyone but yourself and...!

553
00:29:16.520 --> 00:29:17.020
Sanji...

554
00:29:17.110 --> 00:29:18.940
Yes...?

555
00:29:19.610 --> 00:29:21.110
Both of you get out of my sight

556
00:29:21.110 --> 00:29:27.510
before I wring your necks!

557
00:29:27.510 --> 00:29:28.780
Okay, so...

558
00:29:29.250 --> 00:29:30.010
Correct me if I'm wrong,

559
00:29:30.270 --> 00:29:32.540
but doesn't the Log Pose work
better when it's not broken?!

560
00:29:32.540 --> 00:29:35.040
Oh no... Our log pose is ruined!

561
00:29:35.040 --> 00:29:36.510
Calm yourselves...

562
00:29:36.510 --> 00:29:37.380
I will give you my own...

563
00:29:37.800 --> 00:29:40.300
...as a "thank you"
for helping Laboon.

564
00:29:47.810 --> 00:29:49.810
Oh good, I'm not dead...

565
00:29:52.440 --> 00:29:54.110
Hello, dear lady.

566
00:29:54.110 --> 00:29:55.570
Allow me to
help you to your feet.

567
00:29:55.570 --> 00:29:56.610
Oh, thank you.

568
00:29:56.610 --> 00:29:57.820
Nice day, don't you think?

569
00:29:57.820 --> 00:29:58.610
Hey!

570
00:29:59.240 --> 00:30:00.530
We need a favor.

571
00:30:04.160 --> 00:30:05.450
Whisky Peak?

572
00:30:05.780 --> 00:30:06.990
Huh. That's a funny name.

573
00:30:06.990 --> 00:30:08.080
So what is it?

574
00:30:08.080 --> 00:30:10.830
That's where we live... Um, sir.

575
00:30:10.830 --> 00:30:11.750
How were you stranded?

576
00:30:12.010 --> 00:30:12.960
Where's your ship?

577
00:30:12.960 --> 00:30:15.420
Well... It was destroyed.

578
00:30:16.040 --> 00:30:18.850
Asking us for a
ride is pushing it, Mr. 9;

579
00:30:18.920 --> 00:30:20.130
especially after you
tried to kill the whale?

580
00:30:20.550 --> 00:30:21.680
What's with the wardrobe?

581
00:30:21.710 --> 00:30:22.470
What are you supposed to be?

582
00:30:22.470 --> 00:30:24.180
I am a king!

583
00:30:25.260 --> 00:30:26.220
You're lying.

584
00:30:26.640 --> 00:30:27.810
No, please!

585
00:30:27.910 --> 00:30:29.010
We can't say!

586
00:30:29.010 --> 00:30:30.210
She's right.

587
00:30:30.210 --> 00:30:32.540
You have to believe us, our only
motive here is getting home.

588
00:30:32.610 --> 00:30:34.980
We'd tell you everything
if we could, it's just that...

589
00:30:35.210 --> 00:30:37.250
..."mystery" is
our company's motto.

590
00:30:37.310 --> 00:30:38.910
You see, we have
to be mysterious!

591
00:30:38.910 --> 00:30:39.910
It's sort of a rule...

592
00:30:39.980 --> 00:30:41.580
We have confidence
in your character.

593
00:30:41.710 --> 00:30:43.360
Can't you give us
the same courtesy?!

594
00:30:43.610 --> 00:30:44.780
Please! We're begging you!

595
00:30:44.810 --> 00:30:46.050
Show some mercy!

596
00:30:46.110 --> 00:30:47.050
Don't do it...

597
00:30:47.410 --> 00:30:49.610
These two fools are
dishonest to the core.

598
00:30:49.610 --> 00:30:51.050
They can't be trusted.

599
00:30:51.210 --> 00:30:52.210
Listen...

600
00:30:52.210 --> 00:30:53.280
I should mention that
our Log Pose was broken,

601
00:30:53.280 --> 00:30:56.170
and we don't have another one,
so still wanna ride with us?

602
00:30:56.500 --> 00:30:57.780
What...?! You broke it?!

603
00:30:57.910 --> 00:30:58.580
That was mine!

604
00:30:58.710 --> 00:30:59.910
Those aren't cheap, you know?!

605
00:30:59.910 --> 00:31:00.750
You're stuck here too?!

606
00:31:01.010 --> 00:31:02.350
How long were you
gonna make us beg

607
00:31:02.350 --> 00:31:03.760
before you bothered
to tell us?!

608
00:31:04.130 --> 00:31:05.550
Oh... Sorry... I forgot.

609
00:31:05.550 --> 00:31:08.720
Crocus gave us
his Log Pose, so...

610
00:31:09.560 --> 00:31:11.720
Oh! Please have pity on us!

611
00:31:12.100 --> 00:31:14.690
That lousy bitch!
She tricked us!

612
00:31:15.020 --> 00:31:16.520
It's fine...
You can ride with us.

613
00:31:17.940 --> 00:31:19.400
You said your home
is called Whisky Peak?

614
00:31:19.400 --> 00:31:20.570
Let's go there.

615
00:31:21.320 --> 00:31:23.850
Why?! These two are obviously
some pretty shady characters.

616
00:31:24.310 --> 00:31:25.530
Why would we
take them anywhere?!

617
00:31:26.950 --> 00:31:27.980
It's fine... Don't
sweat the small stuff.

618
00:31:28.010 --> 00:31:28.990
We'll be all right.

619
00:31:28.990 --> 00:31:30.510
Choose your route carefully.

620
00:31:30.510 --> 00:31:31.680
Once you head out from here,

621
00:31:31.680 --> 00:31:33.960
you'll be committed
to that course.

622
00:31:33.960 --> 00:31:35.010
That's okay.
If we don't like it,

623
00:31:35.050 --> 00:31:36.790
we'll try a different
route next time.

624
00:31:37.330 --> 00:31:38.710
I see...

625
00:31:39.250 --> 00:31:41.090
Okay...! It's time we get going!

626
00:31:42.460 --> 00:31:43.750
Now that me and
Laboon have an understanding,

627
00:31:43.810 --> 00:31:45.550
I can leave with
a clear conscience!

628
00:31:45.930 --> 00:31:48.300
Just who on earth do
you think you are anyway?

629
00:31:48.300 --> 00:31:50.140
What's that...? Me?

630
00:31:50.560 --> 00:31:52.720
Oh, I'm the man who'll
be King of the Pirates!

631
00:31:57.190 --> 00:31:58.770
Not too bright, this one...

632
00:32:01.650 --> 00:32:03.190
Should be good to go.

633
00:32:03.190 --> 00:32:05.240
The Log Pose has had plenty
of time to store the route.

634
00:32:05.860 --> 00:32:08.320
The needle should be pointing in
the same direction as the map.

635
00:32:09.780 --> 00:32:11.740
It's pointing
directly to Whisky Peak.

636
00:32:12.240 --> 00:32:14.080
See ya, pops!

637
00:32:14.080 --> 00:32:15.660
Thanks again for the
Log Pose! Take care!

638
00:32:15.770 --> 00:32:17.170
Have a safe trip, my boy!

639
00:32:17.200 --> 00:32:18.600
I'm off, Laboon!

640
00:32:18.670 --> 00:32:21.040
Be ready to fight
when I get back!

641
00:32:25.170 --> 00:32:27.130
Next stop, Whisky Peak!

642
00:32:27.130 --> 00:32:29.510
Ready gang...?!
Let's set sail...

643
00:32:49.160 --> 00:32:50.230
I wonder...

644
00:32:50.260 --> 00:32:52.560
Luffy and his
exuberant crew could be

645
00:32:52.560 --> 00:32:54.040
the very pirates
we've been waiting for...

646
00:32:54.890 --> 00:32:57.700
That young captain
sure has a way about him.

647
00:32:57.790 --> 00:33:00.260
It's uncanny really...

648
00:33:01.040 --> 00:33:02.250
Won't you agree...

649
